  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let tension in copper and steel wires are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>cu</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>st</mi></msub></math>. Assuming same strain (due to heavy plank) we note that<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext>Y</mtext><mtext>steel</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msub><mo>⁡</mo><mtext>st</mtext></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>Δ</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<br /><br />or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msub><mo>⁡</mo><mtext>st</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msub><mo>⁡</mo><mtext>cu</mtext></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><msub><mo>⁡</mo><mtext>steel</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><msub><mo>⁡</mo><mtext>cu</mtext></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mtext>given</mtext></mfenced><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace></math>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msub><mo>⁡</mo><mtext>st</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msub><mo>⁡</mo><mtext>cu</mtext></msub></math><br /><br />Further,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>st</mi></msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>cu</mi></msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>given</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br /><u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0014785_AnsExp1_1.jpg\" style=\"width: 310px; height: 216px;\" /></strong></u><br /><br />or<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>cu</mi></msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>cu</mi></msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>&nbsp;or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>cu</mi></msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math><br /><br />And therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>st</mi></msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>cu</mi></msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math><br /><br />Thus&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>cu</mi></msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>&nbsp;is &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>cu</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kgf</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>245</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>&nbsp;</p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>st</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kgf</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>490</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p>",
